This approach ensures that:

Records are deduplicated based on event_id within each partition (_created_at).
Existing records are updated if they match on both event_id and _created_at.
New records are inserted if they don't exist in the target table.
The partitioning by _created_at is maintained, which is crucial for performance in large datasets.



